{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "חלוץ", :translit "chalutz", :gloss "armed/girded (or: one who removes the shoe)"} {:he "ב' במסרה", :translit "bet bi-masrah", :gloss "two in the Masorah"} {:he "חלוץ הנעל", :translit "chelutz ha-na'al", :gloss "removal of the shoe (Deut 25:9)"} {:he "כל היוצא למלחמת בית דוד גט כריתות כותב לאשתו", :translit "kol ha-yotzei le-milchemet beit david get keritot kotev le-ishto", :gloss "all who go out to the war of the House of David write a bill of divorce for his wife"} {:he "שלא תזקק ליבם", :translit "she-lo tizdok le-yavam", :gloss "so that she not be claimed by the yavam"} {:he "ולא תצטרך לחלוץ מן היבם", :translit "ve-lo titzterach le-chalotz min ha-yavam", :gloss "and not need chalitzah from the yavam"} {:he "ושמעינן מכאן שגם משה עשה כן", :translit "u-shema'inan mi-kan she-gam moshe asah ken", :gloss "and we hear from here that Moses too did so"} {:he "וממנו למד דוד", :translit "u-mimenu lamad david", :gloss "and from him David learned"} {:he "ועבר לכם כל חלוץ", :translit "ve-avar lachem kol chalutz", :gloss "and every armed man shall cross over for you (Num 32:21)"} {:he "חלוץ הנעל", :translit "chelutz ha-na'al", :gloss "removal of the shoe"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["חלוץ" "חלוץ הנעל"]} {:kind :other, :note "Wordplay linking חלוץ (armed soldier, Num 32:21) to חלוץ הנעל (shoe-removal in chalitzah, Deut 25:9) via shared root ח-ל-ץ"}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'מלחמת בית דוד' alludes to Shabbat 56a, where Rav Yehudah states that David's soldiers would write a bill of divorce for their wives before going to battle, so that their wives would be free to remarry and would face neither yibum nor chalitzah if the husband fell. The Ba'al HaTurim reasons that Moses must have established this same practice first, since Numbers 32:21 addresses soldiers going to war using the word חלוץ, which by a verbal link to חלוץ הנעל (Deuteronomy 25:9) signals that Moses preempted the problem of chalitzah for soldiers' wives. David then learned the practice from Moses's precedent.", :sources ["Shabbat 56a" "Numbers 32:21" "Deuteronomy 25:9"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["חלוץ" "חלוץ הנעל"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "חלוץ", :refs ["Numbers 32:21" "Numbers 32:27" "Numbers 32:29" "Deuteronomy 25:10"], :n 4, :lens :exact} {:phrase "חלוץ הנעל", :refs ["Deuteronomy 25:10"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Wordplay linking חלוץ (armed soldier, Num 32:21) to חלוץ הנעל (shoe-removal in chalitzah, Deut 25:9) via shared root ח-ל-ץ", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:32:31.824982267Z", :model "glm-5.2"}